    "lawCode": "Amd §6, Chap 987 of 1971",
    "lawSection": "Education",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S3516\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend chapter 987 of the laws of 1971\namending the education law and the civil practice law and rules\nrelating to the regulation and practice of certain professions; and to\ncontinue the dental society of the state of New York, in relation to\ncounting representation in the New York state dental association\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\n\nTo eliminate the requirement that members in one local component\ndental society be counted for representation purposes in the local\ncomponent dental society where they practice.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1 deletes the requirement that members in one local component\ndental society be counted for representation purposes in the local\ncomponent dental society where they practice.\n\nSection 2 makes the bill effective immediately upon enactment.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThe New York State Dental Association is entering into a new\nintegrated computerized membership system called Aptify that is\nmanaged by the American Dental Association. The Aptify system is\nincapable of tracking and categorizing members of local component\ndental societies for two different purposes. Aptify can only\naccommodate membership in the local component dental society where the\ndentist is actually a member. It cannot track or reflect\nrepresentation for voting purposes in a different local component\ndental society.\n\nAll local component dental societies of the New York State Dental\nAssociation will be transitioning to the Aptify system along with the\nAmerican Dental Association and the New York State Dental Association.\nIn order to make this transition possible, the statute governing the\nNew York State Dental Association and its local component dental\nsocieties must be amended to eliminate the requirement that voting\nrepresentation be tracked differently from actual membership in a\nlocal component dental society. This change affects less than one\nhundred dentists and results in no change to any local component\ndental society representation or voting rights in either the New York\nState Dental Association or the American Dental Association.\nTherefore, the change is merely a housekeeping item that is necessary\nto allow implementation of the unified Aptify membership system.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNone.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone to the state.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately upon enactment into law.\n",
